TITLE 'APEEL FILE: PEEL18CV8 SYNCHRONIZATION CIRCUITS'
DESIGNER: 'JAMES PEEL'
DATE: '9/13/88'

Description

This example demonstrates the usefulness of the feedback from the OR gate.
Eigth asynchronous signals can be synchronized by using the circuit below.
Each FEED_OR feedback first latches the signal. This signal is then clocked
out on the next rising edge of the clock from pin 1. The RESET pin is used
to clear the latches and registers.

End_Desc;

PEEL18CV8


 CLK pin 1;
I1 pin 2;
I2 pin 3;
I3 pin 4;
I4 pin 5;
I5 pin 6;
I6 pin 7;
I7 pin 8;
I8 pin 9;
RESET pin 11;
IOC (12 'SYNC8' Pos OutReg Feed_Or)
IOC (13 'SYNC7' Pos OutReg Feed_Or)
IOC (14 'SYNC6' Pos OutReg Feed_Or)
IOC (15 'SYNC5' Pos OutReg Feed_Or)
IOC (16 'SYNC4' Pos OutReg Feed_Or)
IOC (17 'SYNC3' Pos OutReg Feed_Or)
IOC (18 'SYNC2' Pos OutReg Feed_Or)
IOC (19 'SYNC1' Pos OutReg Feed_Or)

AC NODE 21
SP NODE 22

Define

EQUATIONS

SYNC1.D := !RESET & CLK & I1 # 
           !RESET & !CLK & SYNC1 #
           !RESET & I1 & SYNC1 ;
SYNC2.D := !RESET & CLK & I2 #
           !RESET & !CLK & SYNC2 #
           !RESET & I2 & SYNC2;
SYNC3.D := !RESET & CLK & I3 #
           !RESET & !CLK & SYNC3 #
           !RESET & I3 & SYNC3;
SYNC4.D := !RESET & CLK & I4 #
           !RESET & !CLK & SYNC4 #
           !RESET & I4 & SYNC4;
SYNC5.D := !RESET & CLK & I5 #
           !RESET & !CLK & SYNC5 #
           !RESET & I5 & SYNC5;
SYNC6.D := !RESET & CLK & I6 #
           !RESET & !CLK & SYNC6 #
           !RESET & I6 & SYNC6;
SYNC7.D := !RESET & CLK & I7 #
           !RESET & !CLK & SYNC7 #
           !RESET & I7 & SYNC7;
SYNC8.D := !RESET & CLK & I8 #
           !RESET & !CLK & SYNC8 #
           !RESET & I8 & SYNC8;

SYNC8.And = 1;
SYNC7.And = 1;
SYNC6.And = 1;
SYNC5.And = 1;
SYNC4.And = 1;
SYNC3.And = 1;
SYNC2.And = 1;
SYNC1.And = 1;